0..75 Comment "// A returner\'s row is a row of interfaces: each interface\'s name holds its"
76..144 Comment "// signature, no name twice, the names in no order of their own. Two"
145..215 Comment "// rows that list the same interfaces in different orders are one row,"
216..294 Comment "// sequencing joins the rows of the computations it runs, and a computation is"
295..365 Comment "// read where a row holding more is asked: the set operations of a row"
366..440 Comment "// (Hillerström and Lindley, \"Liberating Effects with Rows and Handlers\","
441..499 Comment "// Type-Driven Development 2016, § 2). What refuses is in"
500..550 Comment "// `../../pathological/control/effect-rows.gandr`."
551..553 Comment "//"
554..569 Comment "// - see: #2269"
